Sources of the Oakland RCV corpus and of the Dominion converter's tests, and their terms of use

This notice records the terms of the Oakland corpus's sources as read on 2026-11-09 and those of
the Dominion converter's tests as read on 2026-11-10.  The repository holds no file of either.  It
holds each file's URL, size, and SHA-256 in manifest.json, the per-round figures that README.md
tabulates, the originally certified District 4 figures that district4.py quotes, and the figures of
the Division of Elections' 2024 report that dominion_check.py holds.  fetch.py and
dominion_check.py --fetch download each file from its URL in the manifest into a local directory
that Git ignores.

Alameda County Registrar of Voters

The RCV detailed reports come from https://www.alamedacountyca.gov/rovresults/rcv/, and the
Registrar's presentation on the 2022 District 4 error comes from
https://www.acgov.org/board/bos_calendar/documents/RankedChoiceVotingTallyPresentation.pdf.
Oakland City Charter section 1105(i) requires the summary, ballot image, and comprehensive reports
of each ranked choice voting election to be made available to the public via the internet.  The
County's Legal / Disclaimers page, https://acgov.org/government/legal.htm, states under
"Intellectual Property": "The content of ACGOV web pages is copyrighted, and contains some third
party images/graphics that are used with permission.  Users are notified, therefore, that one
should presume the need to obtain permission from the copyright holder before reproducing or
otherwise using images/graphics from this website.  You are not entitled to copy logos, images,
photographs, software or other material for personal or other non-County use which is made
available through the County site that is contrary to any law, infringes on any copyright,
trademark, or other proprietary right of any party without prior written permission of the
County."  The corpus downloads the County's files for local use and does not redistribute them.

For the elections in the corpus, the County releases its own cast vote records on request.  The
page of the November 5, 2024 election links to the County's public records request form, and the
results page of the November 3, 2026 election links to a request form.  A search of the County's
election and results pages and of the web on 2026-11-09 found no County cast vote record of these
elections at a public URL, so the corpus contains none.

D. Otis, Single winner ranked choice voting CVRs (Harvard Dataverse)

The cast vote records come from Deb Otis, "Single winner ranked choice voting CVRs", Harvard
Dataverse, version 25 (2025-09-24), https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/AMK8PJ.  The dataset's license, as
the Dataverse API reports it, is CC0 1.0
(http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0).  fetch.py downloads each file in its original
CSV form through https://dataverse.harvard.edu/api/access/datafile/<id>?format=original.  Harvard
Dataverse's general terms of use are at
https://support.dataverse.harvard.edu/harvard-dataverse-general-terms-use.  That page returned
HTTP 403 to scripted requests, so their text is not quoted here.  README.md and manifest.json cite
the dataset by its DOI and version.

State of Alaska, Division of Elections

The Dominion converter's tests read the Division's cast vote record exports and RCV reports of the
special general election of August 16, 2022 and the general elections of November 8, 2022 and
November 5, 2024, from the results pages that https://www.elections.alaska.gov/election-results/
lists.  The Division's Website Disclaimer, https://www.elections.alaska.gov/website-disclaimer/,
states under "General": "This is a State of Alaska web site, provided as a public service.
Government personnel and the general public may use this system to review the publicly available
government information contained herein."  Under "Disclaimer of Liability" it states: "The
information and data included on the Division of Elections web pages have been compiled by State
staff from a variety of sources, and are subject to change without notice.  The Division of
Elections makes no warranties or representations whatsoever regarding the quality, content,
completeness, or adequacy of such information and data.  In any situation where the official
printed publications of the Division of Elections differ from the text contained in this system,
the official printed documents take precedence."  The page's other sections disclaim reliability
and damages and set the rules of the Division's social media, and none of them states a condition
on copying the files.

GlobalSign

The Division's server does not send the intermediate certificate that issued its own, so
dominion_check.py --fetch adds GlobalSign's certificate "GlobalSign GCC R46 OV TLS CA 2025", from
http://secure.globalsign.com/cacert/gsgccr46ovtlsca2025.crt, to the system's roots for its requests.
GlobalSign lists its CA certificates at https://support.globalsign.com/ca-certificates, whose footer
states "© 2026 GlobalSign.  All Rights Reserved." and links GlobalSign's legal repository,
https://www.globalsign.com/en/repository.  The repository's Relying Party Agreement, version 1.2,
https://www.globalsign.com/en/repository/GlobalSign_Relying_Party_Agreement.pdf, states in section
3: "This Agreement becomes effective between GlobalSign and the Party ('the Relying Party') when the
latter submits a certificate validation query or otherwise uses or relies upon any information
provided by GlobalSign through its website."  Section 6 states: "The Relying Party is solely
responsible for deciding whether or not to rely on the information provided by GlobalSign."

City and County of San Francisco, Department of Elections, through the Internet Archive

San Francisco's Department of Elections published Dominion's document "CVR export file format",
printed to PDF on 2020-10-21, with the cast vote record export of its election of November 8, 2022,
at https://www.sfelections.org/results/20221108/data/N22_DSuite_CVRExportFormat.pdf.  The tests
read the Internet Archive's capture of 2025-08-26 through
https://web.archive.org/web/20250826234510id_/https://www.sfelections.org/results/20221108/data/N22_DSuite_CVRExportFormat.pdf.
The document's four pages carry no copyright notice or other statement of terms.  On 2026-11-10
www.sfelections.org returned HTTP 403 to scripted requests for https://www.sfelections.org/ and
https://www.sfelections.org/results/20221108/, so San Francisco's terms are not quoted here.  The
Internet Archive's Terms of Use, https://archive.org/about/terms.php, returned to a scripted request
a page that loads its text with JavaScript and holds none of it, so their text is not quoted here.
The Internet Archive's help page "Rights", https://help.archive.org/help/rights/, states: "The
Internet Archive does not make guarantees as to the copyright status of items on archive.org and
cannot guarantee information posted on item details or collection pages regarding copyright or other
intellectual property rights.  Our Terms of Use require that users make use of the Internet
Archive's Collections at their own risk and ensure that such use is non-infringing and in accordance
with all applicable laws."
